Jāmbavān rises asking where seen who steals Sītā --- Jāmbavān vaunts irresistible Rāma Lakṣmaṇa arrows --- Sampāti promises tale of hearing abduction --- Sampāti tells aged fall fed by son Supārśva --- Sampāti tells hungry rebuke and son truthful reply --- Supārśva blocks Mahēndra gate seeking meat --- Supārśva sees black Rāvaṇa bearing sun-bright woman --- Supārśva spares polite asker and learns Rāvaṇa from Siddhas --- Sampāti offers speech counsel and urges swift resolve
